<!-- ================================================================
     SECTION 1 — THE BUILD
     ================================================================ -->
<section class="sec hero" id="build">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">

    <p class="eyebrow dot">Case Study 01 · WordPress Ecommerce</p>
    <h1>MILANU<br><em>shoppable video</em> commerce</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      A premium Bangladeshi fashion label with a catalogue people <b>watched</b> but didn't buy.
      We rebuilt it around the way BD shoppers actually shop — <b>thumb-scrolling, video-first,
      COD-and-WhatsApp</b> — and wrote a custom plugin to do what no off-the-shelf tool would.
    </p>

    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip k">WordPress</span>
      <span class="chip k">WooCommerce</span>
      <span class="chip">Elementor</span>
      <span class="chip">WoodMart</span>
      <span class="chip">Custom Plugin</span>
      <span class="chip">YouTube Data Flow</span>
      <span class="chip">Mobile-first</span>
      <span class="chip chip-flag">Bangladesh <svg class="flag" viewBox="0 0 20 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="20" height="12" rx="1.6" fill="#006A4E"/><circle cx="8.4" cy="6" r="4.1" fill="#F42A41"/></svg></span>
    </div>
    </div><!-- /.hero-copy -->

    <div class="hero-visual">
    <!-- ---------- 3D CONCEPT #1 ---------- -->
    <div class="stage3d" id="stage" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="floor"></div>
      <div class="mock3d" id="mock">
        <div class="mock3d-inner">
          <div class="screen">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="url">milanubd.com</span></div>
            <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="MILANU storefront hero — four models in premium printed lawn" width="1150" height="719">
          </div>
          <div class="fchip c1"><span class="dotg"></span><span><small>COD Ready</small>Cash on Delivery</span></div>
          <div class="fchip c2">
            <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#D45405" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m23 7-7 5 7 5V7z"/><rect x="1" y="5" width="15" height="14" rx="2"/></svg>
            <span><small>Style in Motion</small>13 shoppable reels</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fchip c3"><span><small>Best seller</small><span class="pl">৳ 1,550</span></span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mock-note">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 9l-3 3 3 3M9 5l3-3 3 3M15 19l-3 3-3-3M19 9l3 3-3 3M2 12h20M12 2v20"/></svg>
    </p>
    </div><!-- /.hero-visual -->
    </div><!-- /.hero-grid -->

    <!-- ---------- snapshot stats ---------- -->
    <div class="stats" role="list">
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="9">9</b><span>Collections</span></div>
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="13">13</b><span>Shoppable reels</span></div>
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="70">70</b><span>Images shipped</span></div>
      <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b data-count="1" data-suffix=" plugin">1</b><span>Written from scratch</span></div>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- what shipped ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:52px">
      <span class="kicker">What shipped</span>
      <h2>Nine collections, one <em style="font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-weight:400">continuous</em> buying path</h2>
      <p class="lede">Every piece of this storefront was tuned for a shopper on a ৳15,000 Android phone with
        4 bars of 4G. Nothing decorative survived unless it helped someone buy.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g3">
      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="3" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1.5"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Catalogue</span>
        <h4>9 live collections</h4>
        <p>Summer Kaaftan, Solids, Premium Summer Cotton, Premium Soft Silk, New Arrivals, Luxury Pret,
          Kurti, Embroidered Pret, Co-ords — each tile carries its own product count so nothing looks empty.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20.6 12.6 12 21.2l-9.2-9.2V3.5h8.5z"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="7.5" r="1.5"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Merchandising</span>
        <h4>Discount-led grids</h4>
        <p>Trending and Best Seller rails run live WooCommerce queries with <mark>-28%</mark> strike-through
          pricing, "Hot" badges and variation swatches — price psychology visible at a glance.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 2v6m0 8v6M2 12h6m8 0h6"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3.2"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Sizing</span>
        <h4>Real size runs, not S/M/L</h4>
        <p>Swatch labels map to the ranges BD women actually buy in —
          <b>34-38 = S · 40-42 = L · 44-46 = XXL · 48-52 = 3XL</b> — which removes the #1 reason
          fashion carts get abandoned.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 2 3 7v10l9 5 9-5V7z"/><path d="M3 7l9 5 9-5M12 12v10"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Commerce</span>
        <h4>Ajax cart, wishlist, compare</h4>
        <p>Slide-out cart, wishlist and compare lists, quick-view and quick-shop on every tile — so a
          browser never has to leave the grid to shortlist.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M21 11.5a8.4 8.4 0 0 1-9 8.4 8.6 8.6 0 0 1-3.8-.9L3 21l2-4.8A8.4 8.4 0 0 1 12 3.1a8.4 8.4 0 0 1 9 8.4z"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Checkout</span>
        <h4>COD + WhatsApp ordering</h4>
        <p>Cash on Delivery plus a one-tap WhatsApp order line and multi-channel chat widget
          (Messenger / phone / form). No account required — the way BD fashion actually sells.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 17.3 6.2 21l1.5-6.6L2.8 9.7l6.7-.6L12 3l2.5 6.1 6.7.6-4.9 4.7L17.8 21z"/></svg></div>
        <span class="tag">Trust</span>
        <h4>Reviews wall on the homepage</h4>
        <p>A designed customer-review panel with named buyers, star ratings and avatar cards — social
          proof placed above the footer where hesitation peaks.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- evidence ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:56px">
      <span class="kicker">Evidence · live captures</span>
      <h2>Straight from production</h2>
      <p class="lede">Screenshots taken from the live site at 1440px desktop and 390px mobile.
        Tap any plate to enlarge.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <figure class="plate rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Style in Motion — 13 shoppable reels, each bound to a live WooCommerce product with real view counters">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Style in Motion shoppable reel rail on the MILANU homepage" loading="lazy" width="1150" height="374">
        <figcaption><em>Reels</em> Style in Motion — 13 products, real view counts</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="plate rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Product page — floating portrait reel mounted into the gallery, plus the custom xv Contact + WhatsApp buttons">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="MILANU product page with floating video reel and custom action buttons" loading="lazy" width="1000" height="864">
        <figcaption><em>PDP</em> Floating reel + custom order buttons</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="plate plate-device rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Mobile 390px — sticky bottom tab bar, cart badge, swipe category rail">
        <div class="device-stage">
          <div class="phone">
            <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="MILANU mobile storefront with sticky bottom navigation" loading="lazy" width="560" height="1150">
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption><em>Mobile</em> Sticky tab bar · cart badge · swipe rail</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="plate rv" data-lb="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-cap="Desktop 1440px — the four-model campaign hero with the brand's arch set, category rail below">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="MILANU desktop homepage hero on a live capture" loading="lazy" width="1150" height="719">
        <figcaption><em>Hero</em> Desktop home · 1440px capture</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- technical spotlight ---------- -->
    <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:56px">
      <span class="kicker">Technical spotlight</span>
      <h2>The plugin we had to <em style="font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-weight:400">write ourselves</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">Video commerce plugins existed. None of them bound a product to a vertical reel,
        survived the Elementor editor, stayed keyboard-accessible, and shipped zero extra AJAX.
        So we built <b>Shopable Reel v1.5.0</b> — the custom plugin running on this site today.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3D CONCEPT #2 — pipeline -->
    <div class="flow3d">
      <div class="flow" aria-label="Plugin data pipeline">
        <div class="fstep"><span class="n">01</span><h4>Product bound</h4><p>WooCommerce product + YouTube video joined in one widget</p></div>
        <div class="fstep"><span class="n">02</span><h4>JSON payload</h4><p>Prices, thumbs, view counts printed into <code>data-reels</code></p></div>
        <div class="fstep"><span class="n">03</span><h4>Rail renders</h4><p>Cards output server-side — no layout queries, no flash</p></div>
        <div class="fstep"><span class="n">04</span><h4>YT API boots</h4><p>Promise-cached IFrame API, onReady guarantees mute works</p></div>
        <div class="fstep"><span class="n">05</span><h4>Theatre modal</h4><p>Portrait stage + scrollable side rail, Escape &amp; arrows</p></div>
        <div class="fstep"><span class="n">06</span><h4>View counted</h4><p>Engagement logged per product, feeds the "views" badge</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:22px">
      <div class="code rv">
        <div class="h"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>elementor-widget output · sr-frontend</span></div>
<pre><span class="c">&lt;!-- one widget = tokens + data contract --&gt;</span>
&lt;<span class="k">div</span> class=<span class="s">"sr-devsazzad-wrapper"</span> id=<span class="s">"sr-reel-1"</span>
     style=<span class="s">"--sr-card-w:200px; --sr-card-h:350px;
            --sr-accent:#e74c3c; --sr-side-blur:4px;"</span>
     <span class="t">data-reels</span>=<span class="s">'[{"title":"KISMAT",
        "video_id":"8kzeJhQH7VA",
        "price_html":"&lt;del&gt;৳2,150&lt;/del&gt; ৳1,550",
        "views_formatted":"3K", …}]'</span>&gt;
  &lt;<span class="k">!-- cards ship in the HTML — JS only wires behaviour --&gt;</span>
&lt;/<span class="k">div</span>&gt;</pre>
        <div class="code-cap"><b>Design-token API.</b> The client restyles the rail from Elementor fields —
          no CSS edits, no developer round-trip.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card rv" style="padding:22px">
        <h4 style="font-size:15px">Four bugs we engineered out of existence</h4>
        <ul class="ulist">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Silent video controls.</b> Raw <code>postMessage</code> to a plain iframe fired before the
            player initialised, so mute/autoplay were random. Switched to the real YouTube IFrame API with
            <code>onReady</code> — deterministic every time.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>"Broken in the editor, fine on the site."</b> Elementor re-renders widgets over AJAX
            after load, killing the carousel's listeners. A <code>MutationObserver</code> now re-inits any
            wrapper that appears — self-healing, in both contexts.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Black-on-dark titles.</b> WoodMart's global heading colours out-specified the palette,
            so card titles vanished over dark video. Replaced with a variable-driven colour contract
            (<code>--sr-text-color</code>) and documented the one place <code>!important</code> is
            legitimately required.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Choppy rail scrolling.</b> Native smooth-scroll can't be eased consistently across
            browsers, so the rail uses a custom <code>requestAnimationFrame</code> scroller with an
            <em>easeInOutCubic</em> curve — 60fps on mid-range Android.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- floating reel explainer -->
    <div class="card rv" style="margin-top:14px;padding:22px">
      <div class="grid g2" style="gap:22px">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:12px">Product page · floating reel</span>
          <h3>The reel that follows the product</h3>
          <p style="font-size:13.8px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:10px">
            On every product page a vertical reel mounts <b>inside the image gallery</b> so shoppers see the
            garment move while they read the size chart. It starts minimised at
            <b>160px desktop / 120px mobile</b>, expands to a full theatre, can be dragged anywhere with
            pointer events, and degrades to a fixed corner position when a theme has no gallery container
            to attach to.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="ulist" style="margin-top:0">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Selector-based mounting</b> — targets <code>#main_images_product</code>, falls back to
            <code>.woocommerce-product-gallery</code>, then to fixed positioning.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Drag without breaking playback</b> — a transparent overlay handles the gesture so the
            video underneath stays tappable.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Portrait-native</b> — <code>aspect-ratio:9/16</code>, matching how the label shoots.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
            <span><b>Escape closes it, not the browser.</b> Arrow keys change reel; overlay click does
            nothing that surprises.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================================================================
     SECTION 2 — THE IMPACT
     ================================================================ -->
<section class="sec impact" id="impact">
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="kicker">Section 02 · Why this site · Why it matters</span>
      <h2>The problem wasn't the <span style="font-family:var(--serif);font-style:italic;font-weight:400">clothes</span>.<br>It was the proof.</h2>
      <p class="lede">A ৳1,550 soft-silk suit is an emotional purchase, and a still photo can't show drape,
        fall or movement. MILANU had beautiful product — and 13 short videos nobody could buy from.
        The whole build answers one question: <b>how do we turn watching into wanting, and wanting into an order?</b></p>
    </div>

    <div class="ps">
      <article class="psrow rv">
        <div class="p">
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Problem</span>
          <h4>Static grids under-sell fabric</h4>
          <p>Shoppers couldn't tell soft silk from summer cotton, so the premium pieces lost to cheaper
            lookalikes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s">
          <div class="arw"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12l7 7 7-7"/></svg></div>
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Solution</span>
          <h4>Shoppable reels, product-bound</h4>
          <p>Each reel is a WooCommerce product: live price, discount badge, thumbnail, view count, and a
            one-tap jump to the buy box.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="psrow rv">
        <div class="p">
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Problem</span>
          <h4>BD shoppers don't "add to cart" first</h4>
          <p>They ask a question. No chat channel, no COD, no size clarity = a DM to a Facebook page and a
            lost session.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s">
          <div class="arw"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12l7 7 7-7"/></svg></div>
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Solution</span>
          <h4>Hand-coded order channels</h4>
          <p>A custom button module ships Contact&nbsp;Us + WhatsApp on the buy box — shine-sweep on hover,
            22px radius, tactile press states, and a reduced-motion branch.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="psrow rv">
        <div class="p">
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/></svg>Problem</span>
          <h4>A 4-model hero on a 390px screen</h4>
          <p>Wide campaign photography plus a heavy WooCommerce stack risks a storefront that only works
            on the desktop it was designed on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s">
          <div class="arw"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12l7 7 7-7"/></svg></div>
          <span class="lbl"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Solution</span>
          <h4>True mobile parity</h4>
          <p>Sticky bottom tab bar (Home · Shop · Cart · Account · Menu) with a live cart badge, swipeable
            category rails, and a homepage that behaves like an app — not a shrunken website.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- 3D CONCEPT #3 — measured result ---------- -->
    <div class="chartwrap" id="chart">
      <div class="chart-title">
        <h4>Measured on the live site</h4>
        <span>cold cache · headless Chromium · 2026-10-02</span>
      </div>
      <p class="chart-note">Mobile payload vs desktop, and how far the first paint lands — the numbers a
        first-time visitor on 4G actually feels.</p>
      <div class="bars3d" id="bars">
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:82%"><span class="val">4.03 MB</span><div class="fill"></div></div><span class="lbl">Desktop</span></div>
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:68%"><span class="val">3.38 MB</span><div class="fill alt"></div></div><span class="lbl">Mobile</span></div>
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:59%"><span class="val">2.9 s</span><div class="fill dark"></div></div><span class="lbl">FCP desk</span></div>
        <div class="bar3d"><div class="col" style="--h:41%"><span class="val">2.0 s</span><div class="fill alt"></div></div><span class="lbl">FCP mbl</span></div>
      </div>
      <div style="height:30px"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:16px">
      <div class="card rv"><h4>70 images, 40 lazy-loaded</h4>
        <p>A 70-image homepage still ships 16% <em>less</em> data to phones than to desktops — because
          the media strategy is mobile-first, not desktop-shrunk.</p></div>
      <div class="card rv"><h4>Zero-AJAX rendering</h4>
        <p>Reel cards are printed inside the page HTML, so the rail never waits on a request and never
          causes a late layout shift when it appears. 183 total requests for a full storefront.</p></div>
      <div class="card rv"><h4>Engagement is already proving it</h4>
        <p>Reels on the rail carry real counters — <b>9K · 7K · 7K · 5.6K · 5K</b> views. The top-performing
          product is now the one with the most video, not the biggest banner.</p></div>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- roadmap ---------- -->
    <div class="road">
      <div class="roadcol now rv">
        <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Shipped &amp; verified</h4>
        <ul class="rlist">
          <li><b>Custom Shopable Reel plugin v1.5.0</b> — Elementor widget, token API, YouTube IFrame API, MutationObserver hardening.</li>
          <li><b>Floating product-page reel</b> — gallery-mounted, draggable, 160/120px responsive, theatre expand.</li>
          <li><b>Hand-written order-button module</b> — Contact + WhatsApp, shine sweep, press states, reduced-motion.</li>
          <li><b>BD-first commerce</b> — ৳ currency, real size runs, COD, WhatsApp path, no forced login.</li>
          <li><b>Mobile parity</b> — sticky tab bar, cart badge, swipe rails, 16% lighter mobile payload.</li>
          <li><b>Accessibility inside the widget</b> — Escape to close, arrow-key nav, focus rings, aria labels, reduced-motion honoured.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="roadcol next rv">
        <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Next sprint (our own audit)</h4>
        <ul class="rlist">
          <li><b>Reserve every media box.</b> Measured CLS of 0.35 desktop / 0.47 mobile is the single biggest remaining win — fixed aspect-ratio wrappers on hero and grid imagery.</li>
          <li><b>Give every page an H1.</b> Home and Shop currently ship none; only product pages do.</li>
          <li><b>Write meta descriptions &amp; og:image.</b> Facebook shares are how BD fashion travels — right now a shared link has no preview image and no description.</li>
          <li><b>Alt text at 100%.</b> 67% of homepage images and 100% of shop images are missing it.</li>
          <li><b>Compress the outliers.</b> One source PNG weighs 1.87 MB on its own — convert to WebP.</li>
          <li><b>Add LCP preload</b> for the hero slide to push desktop LCP under 2.5s.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ---------- outcome ---------- -->
    <div class="outcome rv">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px">The outcome</p>
          <h3>A catalogue became a channel — and the video is doing the selling.</h3>
          <p>MILANU now has a storefront that shows the fabric moving, prices it in ৳, lets a shopper order
            on WhatsApp or pay on delivery, and works properly on the phone they're actually holding.
            The custom reel plugin turned 13 idle YouTube uploads into 13 shoppable product pages —
            and because we built it as a reusable Elementor widget, every future reel is a five-minute
            content task, not a development ticket.</p>
          <div class="btnrow">
            <a class="btn btn-p" href="https://milanubd.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/><path d="M15 3h6v6M10 14 21 3"/></svg>
              View live site
            </a>
            <a class="btn btn-g" href="#build">Back to top</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="stats" style="margin:0;background:rgba(255,255,255,.12);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.16)">
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b style="color:#fff">13</b><span style="color:rgba(255,246,239,.6)">Shoppable reels</span></div>
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b style="color:#fff">2</b><span style="color:rgba(255,246,239,.6)">Order channels</span></div>
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b style="color:#fff">5</b><span style="color:rgba(255,246,239,.6)">Size grades</span></div>
            <div class="stat" style="background:transparent"><b style="color:#fff">1</b><span style="color:rgba(255,246,239,.6)">Custom plugin</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

